Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:14:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] perf(ui): read the generation label from the entity, with
 no doc_version key

4ac78101 stored the label and resolved it again when doc_version
changed. The #2238 frame-cost rule does not permit a cache key on
doc_version alone. The job now finds its operation entity one time,
when it starts. Each frame reads the label from that entity through the
new model::live_operation_label, which checks World::is_alive first. A
rename shows at once, and a deleted operation shows its name.

Pinned by one_search_for_each_job_and_a_rename_shows_without_another and
a_deleted_operation_shows_its_name_and_no_dead_entity_is_read.

